Package: starillus-desktop
Architecture: all
Depends: pillarium (>= 2.0.0), spacer-greeter (>= 2.0.0), cadet (>= 0.1.0), libreoffice,
         pilot, flatpak, flatpak-xdg-utils, starillus-app-center, starillus-av
Recommends: planet (>= 0.1.0), planet-control-center (>= 0.1.0),
            lightdm, network-manager
Description: Starillus desktop environment (metapackage)
  Starillus is a lightweight Linux desktop based on Pillarius Desktop, which is
  assembled from Pillarium 2.0 (the window manager and desktop shell), Spacer
  (the LightDM greeter) and Cadet (the companion toolkit/applications).
  .
  This metapackage pulls in the complete Starillus desktop in one step:
  .
    sudo apt install starillus-desktop
  .
  Compared to the Pillarius desktop metapackage this adds:
  .
    * pilot           - the Pilot web browser (a fork of Chromium)
    * flatpak         - Flatpak support with Flathub enabled
    * starillus-app-center - central app platform with anti-virus scanning
    * starillus-av    - resident anti-virus daemon (on-access + scheduled scans)
  .
  The optional desktop applications -- Planet (package manager) and Planet
  Control Center (settings) -- are pulled in as recommendations.
